# 2. PROJECT OBJECTIVE

The application investigates whether combining AI-powered phishing detection with email forensics and infrastructure-level intelligence can improve the reliability, explainability and investigation of phishing emails.

The system must go beyond classifying an email as phishing or legitimate.

It should help an analyst understand:

- Why an email appears suspicious.
- Which technical indicators support the assessment.
- What the email headers reveal.
- Whether authentication evidence is present and what it indicates.
- Which candidate IP addresses appear in the routing chain.
- What infrastructure is associated with those IP addresses and domains.
- Whether multiple emails share infrastructure or other observable characteristics.
- What relationships may indicate a possible phishing campaign.
- Which conclusions are supported by evidence and which remain uncertain.

The application is intended to support both practical cybersecurity investigation and rigorous academic experimentation.

Do not make claims of research novelty or detection superiority.

