# 19. SECURITY, PRIVACY AND RELIABILITY

Implement appropriate protections.

### Input security
- Validate uploaded content.
- Limit file sizes and processing time.
- Handle malformed MIME data.
- Never execute attachments.
- Never execute embedded HTML or scripts.
- Treat email headers and bodies as untrusted input.
- Defang suspicious URLs.
- Protect against malicious prompt injection within email content.

### Backend security
- Keep API keys server-side.
- Validate all requests.
- Use safe error responses.
- Add rate limiting where appropriate.
- Prevent arbitrary outbound requests and SSRF.
- Restrict external enrichment to approved providers and validated indicators.
- Do not allow arbitrary URLs extracted from emails to be fetched by the server.
- Avoid sensitive information in logs.

### Privacy
- No permanent email storage by default.
- No automatic third-party transmission of raw email.
- No training on uploaded emails.
- No silent retention.
- Explicit privacy notices.
- Temporary session-scoped processing.

### Reliability
- Handle provider failures independently.
- One failed enrichment service must not break forensic analysis.
- Handle missing evidence gracefully.
- Keep audit-relevant processing metadata without retaining sensitive email contents.
- Add automated tests for critical processing paths.

Do not claim full production security until a proper security review has been performed.

